---
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";
---

<section class="bg-surface-subtle">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHeader num="09" title="Anti-Patterns" sub="What to avoid. Exceptions are allowed, but the reason should be explicit." />

    <div class="anti-grid">
      <div class="anti-pair">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg text-sm leading-relaxed bg-error-subtle border-l-[3px] border-l-error-base">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 text-error-base">Don't</div>
          Use a second accent color alongside #007FFF. It fragments the visual language and confuses the hierarchy.
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg text-sm leading-relaxed bg-success-subtle border-l-[3px] border-l-success-base">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 text-success-base">Do</div>
          Keep #007FFF as the sole accent. Use brand tones (navy, secondary blue) for structural variation.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="anti-pair">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg text-sm leading-relaxed bg-error-subtle border-l-[3px] border-l-error-base">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 text-error-base">Don't</div>
          Use rgba() for tag backgrounds or overlays. Transparency stacking creates unpredictable color shifts.
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg text-sm leading-relaxed bg-success-subtle border-l-[3px] border-l-success-base">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 text-success-base">Do</div>
          Use the lookup table of solid hex equivalents for all tag tints. Rendering stays stable and color remains accurate.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="anti-pair">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg text-sm leading-relaxed bg-error-subtle border-l-[3px] border-l-error-base">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 text-error-base">Don't</div>
          Set UI text to font-weight: 300 or lighter. Thin weights reduce readability at small sizes.
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg text-sm leading-relaxed bg-success-subtle border-l-[3px] border-l-success-base">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 text-success-base">Do</div>
          Body at 400, headings at 600-700. For more presence, use size or an accent treatment, never synthetic bold.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="anti-pair">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg text-sm leading-relaxed bg-error-subtle border-l-[3px] border-l-error-base">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 text-error-base">Don't</div>
          Use hard drop shadows like 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3). They add visual noise and feel heavy.
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg text-sm leading-relaxed bg-success-subtle border-l-[3px] border-l-success-base">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1.5 text-success-base">Do</div>
          Ring shadow 0 0 0 1px var(--surface-muted) or whisper box-shadow at 0.04 opacity. Or simply alternate light/dark sections.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
